\fBfilter_example\&.c\fP\&.
.SS "struct \fBstumpless_entry\fP * stumpless_add_new_param_to_entry (struct \fBstumpless_entry\fP * entry, const char * element_name, const char * param_name, const char * param_value)"

.PP
Creates a new param and adds it to the given element in the given entry\&. If an element with the given name does not exist in the given entry, then one will be created with the new param added to it\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe\fP This function is thread safe\&. A mutex is used to coordinate changes to the entry while it is being modified\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the use of a non-reentrant lock to coordinate changes and the use of memory management functions\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, due to the use of a lock that could be left locked as well as memory management functions\&.
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
release v1\&.6\&.0\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIentry\fP The entry to add the new param to\&.
.br
\fIelement_name\fP The name of the element to add the param to\&. If an element with this name is not found, it will be created\&. Valid name should have printable ASCII characters expect '=', ']' , ''' and should be 32 characters long\&.
.br
\fIparam_name\fP The name of the new param to add\&.
.br
\fIparam_value\fP The value of the new param to add\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The modified entry if no error is encountered\&. If an error is encountered, then NULL is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "struct \fBstumpless_entry\fP * stumpless_copy_entry (const struct \fBstumpless_entry\fP * entry)"

.PP
Creates a copy of an entry\&. Copies of entries are 'deep' in that the copy also copies each of the elements that the original entry has, if any\&. This means that even if the elements or params of the original entry are destroyed, the equivalent ones in this entry will still be valid\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe\fP This function is thread safe\&. A mutex is used to coordinate the read of the entry with other accesses and modifications\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the use of a non-reentrant lock to coordinate access and the use of memory management functions to create the copy\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, due to the use of a lock that could be left locked as well as memory management functions\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIentry\fP The entry to copy\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A new entry that is a deep copy of the original\&. If an error is encountered, then NULL is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void stumpless_destroy_entry_and_contents (const struct \fBstumpless_entry\fP * entry)"

.PP
Destroys an entry as well as all elements and params that it contains, freeing any allocated memory\&. \fBThread Safety: MT-Unsafe\fP This function is not thread safe as it destroys resources that other threads would use if they tried to reference this struct\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the destruction of a lock that may be in use as well as the use of the memory deallocation function to release memory\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, as the cleanup of the lock may not be completed, and the memory deallocation function may not be AC-Safe itself\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIentry\fP The entry to destroy\&. 
.RE
.PP

