.SS "bool stumpless_entry_has_element (const struct \fBstumpless_entry\fP * entry, const char * name)"

.PP
True if the given entry has an element with the given name, false otherwise\&. \fBThread Safety: MT-Safe race:name\fP This function is thread safe, of course assuming that name is not changed by another thread during execution\&. A mutex is used to coordinate access to the entry with other accesses and modifications\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the use of a non-reentrant lock to coordinate access\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, due to the use of a lock that could be left locked\&.
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
release v1\&.6\&.0\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIentry\fP The entry to search for the element\&.
.br
\fIname\fP The name of the element to check for\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
True if no error is encountered and the element is found\&. If the element is not found or an error is encountered, then false is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "char * stumpless_entry_to_string (const struct \fBstumpless_entry\fP * entry)"

.PP
Returns all entry's elements in formatted string\&. The character buffer should be freed when no longer is needed by the caller\&.
.PP
