.SS "struct \fBstumpless_entry\fP * vstumpless_load_entry (struct \fBstumpless_entry\fP * entry, enum \fBstumpless_facility\fP facility, enum \fBstumpless_severity\fP severity, const char * app_name, const char * msgid, const char * message, va_list subs)"

.PP
Creates a new entry with the given parameters\&. This function has the same behavior as vstumpless_new_entry, except it does not create a new entry, instead loading an existing struct\&.
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
release v2\&.2\&.0
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIentry\fP The struct to load\&.
.br
\fIfacility\fP The facility code of the entry\&. This should be a \fCSTUMPLESS_FACILITY\fP value\&.
.br
\fIseverity\fP The severity code of the entry\&. This should be a \fCSTUMPLESS_SEVERITY\fP value\&.
.br
\fIapp_name\fP The app_name of the entry\&. If this is NULL, then it will be blank in the entry (a single '-' character)\&. The app name length is restricted to be 48 characters or less\&.
.br
\fImsgid\fP The message id of the entry\&. If this is NULL, then it will be blank in the entry (a single '-' character)\&. The string must be in the ASCII printable range 33 <= character <= 126 as specified in RFC5424\&.
.br
\fImessage\fP The message in the entry\&. This message may contain any format specifiers valid in \fCprintf\fP\&. If this is NULL, then it will be blank in the entry (no characters)\&. This also means that characters such as % need to be escaped as they would be in printf\&.
.br
\fIsubs\fP Substitutions for any format specifiers provided in message\&. The number of substitutions provided must exactly match the number of specifiers given\&. This list must be started via \fCva_start\fP before being used, and \fCva_end\fP should be called afterwards, as this function does not call them\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The loaded entry if no error is encountered\&. If an error is encountered, then NULL is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. 
.RE
.PP

